Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||06-05-2001||03:33 PM||||Ok, will an Getrag 4sp Slave Cylinder fit with my 85 gt 4sp (muncie)?  I really don't think they will but hey its worth trying  THANKS..<P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001<p>[This message has been edited by Bluebottlejunky (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||Steven||06-05-2001||05:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bluebottlejunky:<BR><B>Ok, will an Getrag 4sp Slave Cylinder fit with my 85 gt 4sp (muncie)?  I really don't think they will but hey its worth trying  THANKS..<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't know if that was a misprint or not, but the Getrag was not a 4sp, but a 5sp. The old Muncie 85&86 used a 10035044. The Getrag 86-88 used a 10038878. Remember the GT did not come out till half way thur the model year, and the 5sp Getrag came out roughly half way the the GT run. Or in other words the Getrag did not come out till around the last 1/4 of the production year.<P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
