Z||000005||DRH||06-05-2001||05:35 PM||||Sometimes I use the Fiero Store's online catalog to check interchangeability. Looks like any 85-88 5 speed 4 cyl or an 85-86 4 speed V6. ($79.xx from them) <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A> <P>"The Fiero Store carries new Wagner clutch master and slave cylinders. These units are made to original GM specifications. Fits: 85-86 4Cyl 5spd, 85-86 V6 4spd and 87-88 4Cyl 5spd. CHECK OUT THE TOOLS PAGE TO MAKE THE JOB EASIER! "||||reg||3
Z||000006||Steven||06-05-2001||05:42 PM||||Opps. When you said that you were looking for your 85 GT, I only was looking in the parts catalog for V-6 stuff, never dawned on me that the 85-88 4 cylinder would work, so I never looked at that. Sorry. Next time I will check 4 cylinder stuff too. <P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bluebottlejunky||06-05-2001||05:50 PM||||ok, lol...So I can get a slave cylinder for my car from any 85-88 4sp Fiero?  Thanks everyone! email me if you have one that I could buy..bluebottlejunky@cs.com||||reg||1
Z||000008||DRH||06-05-2001||05:59 PM||||Close... <BR>Any 85-86 4 speed <BR>OR any 85-88 4 cylinder 5 speed (Isuzu)<P>Not trying to split hairs but that will expand your selection quite a bit.<P>What WON'T work: <BR>Any 84 <BR>OR any V6 5 speed (Getrag)<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||06-06-2001||12:52 PM||||Spend the exrta few $$ and buy an original GM slave.  The aftermarket (Wagner, Raybestos, etc) are all the same and are inherently flawed.  The cast iron construction is crap and it makes it nearly impossible to bleed correctly.  An original GM slave bleeds with 2-3 pumps and will last you another 10+ years.  I believe you can get one from <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsdirect.com</A>   You'll need the part # (I don't have it handy), but it should be around $100.<P>  ||||reg||1
